[thin] The inclined lead-in runs down from the roof bearing to the nose and cams the spring out over the receiver ledge during insertion. Its taper and flat crest match the fitted cover.
alternatives: Changing the lead-in angle changes how the leaves spread on entry. Widening the crest changes the tested roof bearing.
